    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "**DNG 3D VIRTUAL TOUR OF THIS PROPERTY AVAILABLE** \r\n\r\nDNG are delighted to present to the market 44 Knocklyon Green, Knocklyon, Dublin 16. \r\n\r\nSituated at the end of a quiet cul-de-sac in this well-established and highly regarded part of Knocklyon, this spacious and light-filled three-bedroom semi-detached family home comes to the market in excellent condition, having undergone extensive upgrading in recent years. Boasting well-proportioned accommodation throughout, together with a west-facing rear garden, the property will undoubtedly appeal to any growing family looking to settle in this popular area. \r\n\r\nThe spacious accommodation briefly comprises a porch, entrance hall, a generous living room with interconnecting door to the open-plan kitchen/dining room, which enjoys direct access to the rear garden via sliding doors. Upstairs, there are three bright and beautifully presented bedrooms (two doubles and one single), along with a family bathroom. \r\n\r\nTo the front, the property is approached by a lawned garden with a paved driveway providing off-street parking. To the rear, the west-facing garden is laid mainly in lawn and features a paved patio area, making it the ideal space to enjoy the sunny orientation throughout the day and well into the evening. \r\n\r\nKnocklyon Green is a peaceful, tree-lined cul-de-sac situated close to a host of local amenities. There is an excellent selection of primary and secondary schools within walking distance, including St. Colmcille's and Sancta Maria. A wide range of shopping facilities are also close by, with Knocklyon Shopping Centre just a short stroll away. Regular bus routes, including the No. 15, provide easy access to the city centre, while the M50 network is just minutes away. \r\n\r\nLeisure facilities are well catered for, with Dodder Valley Park, Ballyboden St. Enda's playing fields and local gym facilities all within easy walking distance."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "GROUND FLOOR - \r\n\r\n\r\nEntrance Porch - \r\nWith sliding door.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall - 3.90m x 1.88m\r\nWelcoming entrance hall with carpet flooring\r\n\r\nLiving Room - 3.90m x 3.91m\r\nBright and spacious living room with integrated solid fuel burning stove, marble mantle and granite hearth\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room - 3.10m x 5.90m\r\nFully fitted kitchen with tiled floor and tiled surround; direct access to the west-facing rear garden via sliding doors\r\n\r\nFIRST FLOOR - \r\n\r\n\r\nLanding - 2.88m x 1.80m\r\nWith hot-press off.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.40m x 4.00m\r\nSpacious double bedroom with built-in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 4.21m x 4.00m\r\nSpacious double bedroom to the front of the property with built-in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 1.65m x 2.05m\r\nSpacious single bedroom to the front of the property.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom - 1.65m x 2.05m\r\nVery stylish, high quality, fully tiled bathroom suite with WC, WHB, bath and heated towel rail"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Outstanding three-bedroom semi-detached family home</li><li> Turnkey condition extensively upgraded in recent years.</li><li> Southwest facing rear garden.</li><li> Side passageway</li><li> Cul-de-sac location</li><li> Green space for kids</li><li> Greenway</li><li> Huge development potential (subject to the relevant planning permission)</li><li> Garden shed with power.</li><li> Double drive parking & off-street parking Close to all local amenities</li><li> GFCH</li><li> Double glazed</li><li> Highly regarded development</li><li> Within walking of a host of excellent primary and secondary schools</li><li> Short drive to the M50</li></ul>"
